  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 🏭 Factory AI Predictive Maintenance — Deploy to Netlify\n",
        "### Built with IBM watsonx · DEMO-MFG-001\n",
        "\n",
        "**This notebook deploys your demo in ~5 minutes — no installs on your computer needed.**\n",
        "\n",
        "| | What happens |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| **Backend** | Runs inside this Colab VM, exposed publicly via Cloudflare Tunnel (free, no account) |\n",
        "| **Frontend** | Built here, deployed to Netlify (free account needed — sign up at netlify.com) |\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "### ▶️ How to run\n",
        "1. Click **Runtime → Run all** (or press `Ctrl+F9`)\n",
        "2. When Cell 5 asks you to log in to Netlify — follow the link, paste the code back\n",
        "3. At the end you get a **live public URL** — share it with anyone\n",
        "\n",
        "> ⚠️ The backend tunnel URL changes every time you restart this Colab session.\n",
        "> When that happens, re-run from Cell 3 onwards and redeploy the frontend.\n",
        "\n",
        "---"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Cell 1 — Clone the repo & install system tools"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# ── 1. Clone your GitHub repo ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "# EDIT THIS LINE: replace with your actual GitHub repo URL\n",
        "REPO_URL = \"https://github.com/Kgotla-AI-Demos/IBM-Pre-Sales-Demo-Builder.git\"\n",
        "# If you get a permission error the repo may be private — use a Personal Access Token:\n",
        "# REPO_URL = \"https://YOUR_PAT@github.com/Kgotla-AI-Demos/IBM-Pre-Sales-Demo-Builder.git\"\n",
        "# Create a PAT at: https://github.com/settings/tokens (check 'repo' scope)\n",
        "\n",
        "import os, subprocess\n",
        "\n",
        "if not os.path.exists(\"/content/repo\"):\n",
        "    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"clone\", REPO_URL, \"/content/repo\"], check=True)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", \"/content/repo\", \"pull\"], check=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "DEMO_DIR = \"/content/repo/demos/new-demo\"\n",
        "print(f\"✅ Repo ready at {DEMO_DIR}\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": None,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Cell 2 — Install Node.js 20 + Netlify CLI"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "%%bash\n",
        "set -e\n",
        "\n",
        "echo \"→ Installing Node.js 20 LTS...\"\n",
        "curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | bash - >/dev/null 2>&1\n",
        "apt-get install -y nodejs >/dev/null 2>&1\n",
        "echo \"   Node $(node --version)  |  npm $(npm --version)\"\n",
        "\n",
        "echo \"→ Installing Netlify CLI...\"\n",
        "npm install -g netlify-cli --silent\n",
        "echo \"   Netlify CLI $(netlify --version)\"\n",
        "\n",
        "echo \"✅ Node + Netlify CLI ready\""
      ],
      "execution_count": None,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Cell 3 — Install Python backend dependencies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "%%bash\n",
        "set -e\n",
        "DEMO_DIR=\"/content/repo/demos/new-demo\"\n",
        "\n",
        "echo \"→ Installing backend Python packages...\"\n",
        "pip install -q -r \"$DEMO_DIR/backend/requirements.txt\"\n",
        "echo \"✅ Backend packages installed\""
      ],
      "execution_count": None,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Cell 4 — Start the backend + expose it with Cloudflare Tunnel\n",
        "\n",
        "> **No account needed.** Cloudflare Tunnel gives a free public HTTPS URL instantly.\n",
        "> The URL will be printed below — copy it, you'll need it in Cell 5."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import subprocess, threading, time, re, sys, os\n",
        "\n",
        "DEMO_DIR = \"/content/repo/demos/new-demo\"\n",
        "BACKEND_DIR = f\"{DEMO_DIR}/backend\"\n",
        "PORT = 8000\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── Install cloudflared ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "if not os.path.exists(\"/usr/local/bin/cloudflared\"):\n",
        "    print(\"→ Downloading cloudflared...\")\n",
        "    subprocess.run([\n",
        "        \"wget\", \"-q\",\n",
        "        \"https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared/releases/latest/download/cloudflared-linux-amd64\",\n",
        "        \"-O\", \"/usr/local/bin/cloudflared\"\n",
        "    ], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run([\"chmod\", \"+x\", \"/usr/local/bin/cloudflared\"], check=True)\n",
        "    print(\"   cloudflared installed\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── Write .env for backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "env_content = \"\"\"DEMO_MODE=mock\n",
        "CORS_ORIGINS=*\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "with open(f\"{BACKEND_DIR}/.env\", \"w\") as f:\n",
        "    f.write(env_content)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── Start FastAPI backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "print(f\"→ Starting FastAPI backend on port {PORT}...\")\n",
        "backend_proc = subprocess.Popen(\n",
        "    [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"uvicorn\", \"main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", str(PORT)],\n",
        "    cwd=BACKEND_DIR,\n",
        "    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n",
        "    stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,\n",
        ")\n",
        "time.sleep(3)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── Start Cloudflare Tunnel ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "print(\"→ Starting Cloudflare Tunnel...\")\n",
        "tunnel_proc = subprocess.Popen(\n",
        "    [\"/usr/local/bin/cloudflared\", \"tunnel\", \"--url\", f\"http://localhost:{PORT}\"],\n",
        "    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n",
        "    stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,\n",
        "    text=True,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── Wait for tunnel URL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "BACKEND_URL = None\n",
        "print(\"   Waiting for tunnel URL\", end=\"\")\n",
        "for _ in range(30):\n",
        "    line = tunnel_proc.stdout.readline()\n",
        "    match = re.search(r'https://[\\w-]+\\.trycloudflare\\.com', line)\n",
        "    if match:\n",
        "        BACKEND_URL = match.group(0)\n",
        "        break\n",
        "    print(\".\", end=\"\", flush=True)\n",
        "    time.sleep(1)\n",
        "\n",
        "print()\n",
        "if BACKEND_URL:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n✅ Backend is live at: {BACKEND_URL}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"   Health check:        {BACKEND_URL}/api/health\")\n",
        "    print(f\"   Interactive docs:    {BACKEND_URL}/docs\")\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n📋 COPY THIS URL — you need it in the next cell:\")\n",
        "    print(f\"   {BACKEND_URL}/api\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"❌ Could not get tunnel URL. Re-run this cell.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Store for next cells\n",
        "import builtins\n",
        "builtins.BACKEND_PUBLIC_URL = BACKEND_URL"
      ],
      "execution_count": None,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Cell 5 — Build the frontend with the backend URL baked in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import subprocess, os, builtins\n",
        "\n",
        "DEMO_DIR = \"/content/repo/demos/new-demo\"\n",
        "FRONTEND_DIR = f\"{DEMO_DIR}/frontend\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── Get backend URL (auto from Cell 4, or paste manually if needed) ──────────\n",
        "BACKEND_URL = getattr(builtins, 'BACKEND_PUBLIC_URL', None)\n",
        "if not BACKEND_URL:\n",
        "    # If Cell 4 was already run before, paste the URL here manually:\n",
        "    BACKEND_URL = input(\"Paste your backend URL from Cell 4 (e.g. https://xyz.trycloudflare.com): \").strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "VITE_API_BASE_URL = f\"{BACKEND_URL}/api\"\n",
        "print(f\"→ Building frontend with VITE_API_BASE_URL={VITE_API_BASE_URL}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── Write .env for Vite build ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "env_content = f\"\"\"VITE_API_BASE_URL={VITE_API_BASE_URL}\n",
        "VITE_DEMO_TITLE=Factory AI Predictive Maintenance — Built with IBM watsonx\n",
        "VITE_DEMO_CLIENT_CODE=DEMO-MFG-001\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "with open(f\"{FRONTEND_DIR}/.env\", \"w\") as f:\n",
        "    f.write(env_content)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── npm install ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "print(\"→ Installing npm packages (this takes ~1 min)...\")\n",
        "result = subprocess.run(\n",
        "    [\"npm\", \"install\", \"--prefer-offline\"],\n",
        "    cwd=FRONTEND_DIR, capture_output=True, text=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "if result.returncode != 0:\n",
        "    print(\"❌ npm install failed:\")\n",
        "    print(result.stderr[-2000:])\n",
        "    raise SystemExit(1)\n",
        "print(\"   npm install complete\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── npm run build ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "print(\"→ Building frontend (vite build)...\")\n",
        "result = subprocess.run(\n",
        "    [\"npm\", \"run\", \"build\"],\n",
        "    cwd=FRONTEND_DIR, capture_output=True, text=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "if result.returncode != 0:\n",
        "    print(\"❌ Build failed:\")\n",
        "    print(result.stdout[-3000:])\n",
        "    print(result.stderr[-2000:])\n",
        "    raise SystemExit(1)\n",
        "\n",
        "dist_size = subprocess.run([\"du\", \"-sh\", f\"{FRONTEND_DIR}/dist\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.split()[0]\n",
        "print(f\"\\n✅ Frontend built successfully! dist/ size: {dist_size}\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": None,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Cell 6 — Deploy frontend to Netlify\n",
        "\n",
        "> **First time only:** Netlify will ask you to log in.\n",
        "> - Click the link it shows\n",
        "> - Log in (or sign up free at netlify.com)\n",
        "> - Authorize → copy the code → paste it back here\n",
        "\n",
        "> **After that**, every deploy is automatic — no login needed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "%%bash\n",
        "set -e\n",
        "FRONTEND_DIR=\"/content/repo/demos/new-demo/frontend\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Authenticate with Netlify (interactive — follow the link shown)\n",
        "echo \"→ Logging in to Netlify (follow the link below)...\"\n",
        "netlify login\n",
        "\n",
        "echo \"\"\n",
        "echo \"→ Deploying to Netlify (production)...\"\n",
        "cd \"$FRONTEND_DIR\"\n",
        "netlify deploy \\\n",
        "  --dir=dist \\\n",
        "  --prod \\\n",
        "  --message=\"Factory AI Demo — IBM watsonx DEMO-MFG-001\" \\\n",
        "  2>&1\n",
        "\n",
        "echo \"\"\n",
        "echo \"✅ Frontend deployed to Netlify!\"\n",
        "echo \"   Look for 'Website URL:' above — that is your shareable demo link.\""
      ],
      "execution_count": None,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Cell 7 — Verify everything is working"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import requests, builtins, json\n",
        "\n",
        "BACKEND_URL = getattr(builtins, 'BACKEND_PUBLIC_URL', None)\n",
        "if not BACKEND_URL:\n",
        "    BACKEND_URL = input(\"Paste backend tunnel URL: \").strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"─\" * 60)\n",
        "print(\"Running verification checks...\")\n",
        "print(\"─\" * 60)\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = [\n",
        "    (\"Health\",     f\"{BACKEND_URL}/api/health\"),\n",
        "    (\"Dashboard\",  f\"{BACKEND_URL}/api/data/dashboard\"),\n",
        "    (\"Equipment\",  f\"{BACKEND_URL}/api/data/equipment\"),\n",
        "    (\"AI Models\",  f\"{BACKEND_URL}/api/ai/models\"),\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "all_ok = True\n",
        "for name, url in checks:\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        r = requests.get(url, timeout=15)\n",
        "        status = \"✅\" if r.status_code == 200 else \"❌\"\n",
        "        if r.status_code != 200:\n",
        "            all_ok = False\n",
        "        print(f\"  {status} {name:<12} {r.status_code}  {url}\")\n",
        "    except Exception as e:\n",
        "        print(f\"  ❌ {name:<12} ERROR: {e}\")\n",
        "        all_ok = False\n",
        "\n",
        "# Test AI endpoint\n",
        "print()\n",
        "print(\"→ Testing AI analyze endpoint (mock mode)...\")\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    r = requests.post(\n",
        "        f\"{BACKEND_URL}/api/ai/analyze\",\n",
        "        json={\"equipment_id\": \"EQ-0012\", \"scenario\": \"bearing_failure\"},\n",
        "        timeout=20,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    if r.status_code == 200 and \"analysis\" in r.json():\n",
        "        data = r.json()\n",
        "        print(f\"  ✅ AI analyze   200  confidence={data.get('confidence')}  mode={data.get('mode')}\")\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        print(f\"  ❌ AI analyze   {r.status_code}  {r.text[:200]}\")\n",
        "        all_ok = False\n",
        "except Exception as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"  ❌ AI analyze   ERROR: {e}\")\n",
        "    all_ok = False\n",
        "\n",
        "print()\n",
        "print(\"─\" * 60)\n",
        "if all_ok:\n",
        "    print(\"✅ All checks passed! Your demo is fully operational.\")\n",
        "    print()\n",
        "    print(\"  Backend : \" + BACKEND_URL)\n",
        "    print(\"  API docs: \" + BACKEND_URL + \"/docs\")\n",
        "    print()\n",
        "    print(\"  Open your Netlify URL in the browser — the demo should be live!\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"❌ Some checks failed. Re-run Cell 4 to restart the backend tunnel.\")\n",
        "print(\"─\" * 60)"
      ],
      "execution_count": None,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 🔁 After a Colab session restart\n",
        "\n",
        "The Colab VM resets after ~12 hours of inactivity. When that happens:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Re-run **Cell 3** (pip install) — fast, uses cache\n",
        "2. Re-run **Cell 4** (start backend + new tunnel URL)\n",
        "3. Re-run **Cell 5** (rebuild frontend with new URL)\n",
        "4. Re-run **Cell 6** (redeploy to Netlify — no login needed this time)\n",
        "\n",
        "Your Netlify site URL **stays the same** every time.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "## 💡 Tips\n",
        "\n",
        "| Tip | Detail |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| Keep Colab open | The backend runs as long as Colab is running. Close it = backend goes offline |\n",
        "| Prevent idle timeout | Click the screen occasionally, or use Colab Pro |\n",
        "| Share the demo | Give your Netlify URL — anyone can open it, no login needed |\n",
        "| Live IBM watsonx.ai | Add your API key in Cell 4's `.env` block and set `DEMO_MODE=live` |\n",
        "\n",
